<LegalPage title="Affiliate disclosure" description="How Dark Romance Fan earns money: affiliate links to Amazon and Bookshop.org, and clearly labelled paid author promotions.">
  <p>Dark Romance Fan is free to read. It pays for itself in two ways, and neither costs you anything extra.</p>

  <h2>Affiliate links</h2>
  <p>Some "Buy" links on this site are affiliate links. If you buy through them, the store pays us a small commission. The price you pay is the same.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Amazon:</strong> As an Amazon Associate I earn from qualifying purchases.</li>
    <li><strong>Bookshop.org:</strong> We earn a commission on books bought through our Bookshop.org links, and Bookshop.org shares part of every sale with independent bookshops.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Commissions never decide which books we list or how they're described. Ratings for spice and darkness come from readers, not from us or the authors.</p>

  <h2>Paid author promotions</h2>
  <p>Authors can pay to feature a book in our newsletter, the Dark Romance Fan newsletter. Paid placements are always labelled <strong>Sponsored</strong>. We check every book before accepting it, and a payment doesn't buy a good review, a place on a reading list or reader ratings.</p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>See our <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a> for how clicks are counted and how to contact us.</p>
</LegalPage>
